&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy. Toast is driven by building a platform that helps restaurants adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: building the businesses they love. Our Finance team serves as a trusted advisor to the company, guiding critical business decisions through insightful analyses &amp;amp; thought partnership with executive leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking an R&amp;amp;D Finance associate to own key aspects of our financial reporting, monthly and quarterly processes, and support critical planning activities within our R&amp;amp;D Finance &amp;amp; Strategy team. In this role, you’ll contribute to the foundation of our finance operations as we advance as a public company, with a focus on enhancing efficiency through process improvements and automation. You’ll work closely with our R&amp;amp;D and Corporate Finance team, and collaborate across functions to deliver essential insights and drive strategic initiatives for our senior R&amp;amp;D leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Toast’s monthly and quarterly financial close processes for the R&amp;amp;D function, including reporting and analysis of budget vs. actual results, forecast updates, and preparation of standard financial packages that provide actionable insights for R&amp;amp;D leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own headcount tracking, reporting, and reconciliation activities for R&amp;amp;D, conducting trend analysis and collaborating closely with Finance, R&amp;amp;D leadership, and Talent Acquisition to align resource planning with strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the financial management for the R&amp;amp;D vendor portfolio, including PO and invoice reconciliation, variance analysis, and trend reporting to ensure alignment with budget and financial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage Toast’s financial systems, tools, and datasets to build and maintain standard reports and analyses, identifying opportunities to improve insight depth and forecast accuracy, specifically tailored to R&amp;amp;D’s unique needs and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and refine existing financial processes for R&amp;amp;D, implementing automation and standardization initiatives to reduce manual workload and create efficiencies across the finance team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with cross-functional teams, to research, analyze, and advise on financial processes and reporting that directly support R&amp;amp;D’s innovation, operational, and financial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work 2 pm - 11 pm IST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of work experience in FP&amp;amp;A, investment banking, consulting, private equity, business operations or accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills including financial modeling, data/trend analysis and manipulation of large datasets, with proven ability to summarize complex data into key takeaways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly proficient in advanced Excel/Google Sheets and PowerPoint/Google Slides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with financial systems, such as WorkDay, Adaptive, Greenhouse, NetSuite, or other similar products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive attitude with high aptitude to learn new things quickly. Team player eager to further develop and grow with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates intellectual curiosity, problem-solving skills, and hunger to continually up-level current approaches and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to work in a collaborative, diverse, inclusive, and open-minded office environment with a desire to contribute to a thriving culture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
