&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*EST OR CST preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Kitchen Operations team owns one of Toast&#39;s most operationally critical and strategically exciting products: the Kitchen Display System (KDS). Deployed across tens of thousands of restaurants, Toast KDS is the connective tissue between front-of-house and back-of-house, routing tickets to the right prep stations, managing order sequencing, and helping kitchens run fast and accurately under pressure. KDS has strong growth across SMB, enterprise, and international segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is KDS in the vast majority of Toast kitchens within the next few years. Getting there means three things: supporting the most sophisticated enterprise kitchen workflows in the market, differentiating through kitchen data and AI-powered operational insights, and growing adoption among the restaurants that still run on paper tickets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership, high-visibility role at the intersection of restaurant operations, hardware-software product, and applied AI. You&#39;ll shape how hundreds of thousands of kitchen workers run their stations every day — and you&#39;ll be the one building the data and agent layer that lets kitchens run smarter, not just faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this roll* (Responsibilities)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive the KDS product strategy — enterprise workflow depth, data differentiation, SMB attach growth, and the agentic AI roadmap — connecting investments to Toast&#39;s kitchen adoption vision and near-term business outcomes including ARR growth, support ticket reduction, and enterprise retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define where agentic AI creates real value in the kitchen: proactive prep time adjustments based on real-time order load, automatic kitchen configuration changes tied to labor schedules or ordering channel mix, intelligent ticket routing and load balancing — and build the investment case to pursue the highest-leverage bets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own KDS delivery end-to-end, working directly with large restaurant groups to translate complex, high-stakes workflow requirements into scalable product decisions that serve the whole market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the KDS kitchen data strategy: define what kitchen efficiency insights should look like for operators at every scale, from API-first analytics for enterprise operators to actionable reporting for SMBs, and sequence the investments to unlock it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and validate the business case for the next-generation KDS strategy — the long-horizon bets that drive future growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you have the right ingredients*? (Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience defining and owning product strategy for a complex, operationally critical product — bonus points if it spans hardware and software and/or have experience in food &amp;amp; beverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative and strategic: you don&#39;t just optimize existing products — you identify the next meaningful bet, make the case for it, and drive it from zero to conviction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and a point of view on AI and agentic product opportunities in operational environments — you don&#39;t need to have shipped an agent, but you should have a clear perspective on where autonomous action creates real value vs. real risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of working directly with enterprise customers, translating nuanced, high-stakes workflow requirements into product decisions that scale well beyond a single logo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts for the SMB operator: you understand what it means to run a restaurant kitchen without a data analyst, an IT team, or a change management budget — and you can build for that reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence to drive alignment without authority across engineering, design, enterprise customer success, sales, and product leadership in a high-stakes, cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
