&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: &lt;/strong&gt;Software Engineer II, Backend — Toast International&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Toronto, ON / Canada Hybrid (Ontario)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level: &lt;/strong&gt;Software Engineer II (SE2)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Toast is driven by building the restaurant platform that helps restaurants adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: building the businesses they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you bready* for a change?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer II on the Toast Tables International team, you will build and scale the cloud services powering modern table management, guest reservations, and front-of-house hospitality for high-volume restaurants across the UK, Europe, and Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work hands-on with distributed microservices in Java and Kotlin—delivering high-impact capabilities such as payment integrations, messaging services, and core platform workflows. You will collaborate with senior engineers, product managers, designers, and mobile/web teammates across North America and Europe to deliver reliable, high-performance features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this roll* (Responsibilities)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, test, and deploy scalable backend microservices using Java / Kotlin and AWS infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement core reservation and guest lifecycle APIs, including international phone validation, geoblocking rules, and two-way notification services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop transactional and payment components for reservation , pre-authorizations, and Card workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data sync endpoints and event consumers connecting&amp;nbsp; with POS order data,&amp;nbsp; fulfillment, and Guestbook profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write comprehensive automated unit, integration, and contract tests to ensure zero-regression releases and high test coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor service health, analyze logs and metrics (Datadog/CloudWatch), and participate in on-call rotations to maintain platform uptime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate in team agile ceremonies, code reviews, and technical design discussions, leveraging modern development tools to ship quality software efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you have the right ingredients*? (Requirements)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of professional backend software development experience building RESTful APIs and distributed systems in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Java or Kotlin (or similar object-oriented languages like C#) and familiarity with modern frameworks (e.g., Spring Boot, Micronaut, Dropwizard).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and writing efficient SQL queries and schema migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with distributed systems concepts, asynchronous messaging (Kafka, Pulsar, or AWS SQS/SNS), and cloud platforms (AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of RESTful API design principles, JSON data modeling, and testing best practices (JUnit, Mockito).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, curiosity to learn restaurant domain workflows, and enthusiasm for collaborating in an agile, cross-functional team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
